    {
      "heading": "From gene to protein",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A gene is read three bases at a time. Each triplet means one amino acid.",
          "write": "triplet → 1 amino acid"
        },
        {
          "say": "First, transcription. In the nucleus, the gene is copied into m R N A.",
          "write": "transcription: DNA → mRNA"
        },
        {
          "say": "R N A uses uracil, U, instead of thymine.",
          "write": "T  →  U",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 280,
            "alt": "DNA triplet TAC copied to mRNA AUG",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 80,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 80,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "T"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 170,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 80,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "A"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 260,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 80,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "C"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 420,
                "y": 100,
                "text": "DNA",
                "size": 22,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 210,
                "y": 130,
                "x2": 210,
                "y2": 170,
                "color": "purple",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 80,
                "y": 180,
                "w": 80,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "A",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 170,
                "y": 180,
                "w": 80,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "U",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 260,
                "y": 180,
                "w": 80,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "G",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 420,
                "y": 220,
                "text": "mRNA",
                "size": 22,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Then translation. A ribosome reads the m R N A and joins amino acids.",
          "write": "translation at ribosome"
        },
        {
          "say": "So 18 bases divided by 3 gives 6 amino acids.",
          "write": "18 ÷ 3 = 6 amino acids"
        },
        {
          "say": "If a mutation changes a triplet, the protein can fold wrong.",
          "write": "mutation → wrong protein"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A gene is the instruction. An allele is one version of it.",
          "write": "gene ≠ allele"
        },
        {
          "say": "Homologous chromosomes are not identical. Sister chromatids are.",
          "write": "sister chromatids = identical"
        },
        {
          "say": "When writing m R N A, swap every T for a U.",
          "write": "no T in RNA"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "DNA, then m R N A, then protein, read in threes.",
          "write": "DNA → mRNA → protein"
        },
        {
          "say": "Body cells have 46. Gametes have 23.",
          "write": "2n = 46,  n = 23"
        },
        {
          "say": "Homologous means same genes, maybe different alleles.",
          "write": "homologous: same genes"
        },
        {
          "say": "A karyotype shows chromosome number, not alleles.",
          "write": "karyotype: number only"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}